## 11. Animal → Young One

```text
Cow : Calf :: Dog : Puppy
```

Examples:

```text
Cat → Kitten
Goat → Kid
Horse → Foal
Sheep → Lamb
Deer → Fawn
Lion → Cub
```

---

## 12. Male → Female

```text
King : Queen :: Man : Woman
```

Examples:

```text
Bull : Cow
Horse : Mare
Lion : Lioness
Tiger : Tigress
Actor : Actress
Prince : Princess
Nephew : Niece
```

---

## 13. Young One → Adult

```text
Calf : Cow :: Puppy : Dog
```

Relationship:

```text
Young ──develops into──> Adult
```

---

## 14. Part → Whole

```text
Wheel : Car :: Page : Book
```

Relationship:

```text
Part ──belongs to──> Whole
```

Examples:

- Finger : Hand
- Leaf : Tree
- Engine : Car
- Chapter : Book
- Keyboard : Computer
- Petal : Flower

---

## 15. Whole → Part

```text
Car : Wheel :: Book : Page
```

Same relationship, opposite direction.

Always identify direction.

---

## 16. Material → Product

```text
Wood : Furniture :: Gold : Jewellery
```

Relationship:

```text
Raw material ──used to make──> Product
```

Examples:

```text
Clay → Pot
Leather → Shoes
Cotton → Cloth
Steel → Machine
Wheat → Bread
```

---

## 17. Product → Material

```text
Paper : Wood :: Glass : Sand
```

Relationship:

```text
Product ──made from──> Material
```

---

## 18. Synonym Analogy

```text
Happy : Joyful :: Sad : Unhappy
```

Relationship:

```text
Word ──similar meaning──> Word
```

Examples:

```text
Big : Large
Fast : Rapid
Begin : Start
Silent : Quiet
Brave : Courageous
```

---

## 19. Antonym Analogy

```text
Hot : Cold :: Day : Night
```

Relationship:

```text
Word ──opposite──> Word
```

Examples:

```text
Rich : Poor
Victory : Defeat
Early : Late
Strong : Weak
Accept : Reject
```

---

## 20. Degree Analogy

Sometimes the relationship is not synonym or antonym but **degree**.

```text
Warm : Hot :: Cool : Cold
```

The second word has stronger intensity.

Other examples:

```text
Like : Love
Annoyed : Angry
Rain : Storm
```

---

## 21. Cause → Effect

```text
Fire : Smoke :: Disease : Fever
```

Relationship:

```text
Cause ──produces──> Effect
```

Examples:

```text
Exercise → Fitness
Rain → Flood
Hard work → Success
Negligence → Accident
```

---

## 22. Effect → Cause

```text
Smoke : Fire :: Fever : Disease
```

Reverse relationship:

```text
Effect ──caused by──> Cause
```

---

## 23. Action → Result

```text
Study : Knowledge :: Exercise : Fitness
```

Relationship:

```text
Action ──produces──> Result
```

---

## 24. Object → Characteristic

```text
Ice : Cold :: Fire : Hot
```

Relationship:

```text
Object ──has characteristic──> Property
```

Examples:

```text
Sugar → Sweet
Lemon → Sour
Feather → Light
Stone → Hard
```

---

## 25. Object → Quality

```text
Gold : Valuable :: Iron : Strong
```

Be careful: the exact quality must match the intended relationship.

---
